  "contentHtml": "\n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>New Delhi: <a href=\"/tag/narayana+health\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Narayana Health</a> has entered into a knowledge-sharing partnership with The <a href=\"/tag/new+development+bank\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">New Development Bank</a> (NDB), to support NDB and its member countries in strengthening smart hospital service capacity by sharing experience in delivering efficient, technology‑enabled and patient‑centric hospital services.The Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between NDB and Narayana Health was signed  by  Dilma Rousseff, President of NDB and Dr Devi Shetty, Founder and Chairman of Narayana Health in Jaipur on the sidelines of the First BRICS Finance Ministers and Central Bank Governors Meeting, the healthcare major said.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M -->\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>It added that the cooperation between the two will focus on digital health, data systems, technology transfer and knowledge sharing.Dr. Devi Shetty, Founder and Chairman, Narayana Health, said, “Through this knowledge sharing collaboration, we look forward to working with NDB and its member countries to support stronger, <a href=\"/tag/technology-enabled+healthcare\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">technology-enabled healthcare</a> systems across emerging economies.”</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>This comes after Dilma Rousseff, NDB President visited Narayana Health City in Bengaluru in March this year,  to observe the institution's innovative approach to providing affordable, high-quality healthcare through patient-focused care and cutting-edge digital technologies.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Online Bureau</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Online Bureau</a>\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/88675629/ETHealthWorld\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ETHealthWorld</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Aug 13, 2026 at 06:55 PM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Aug 13, 2026 at 06:55 PM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">1 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                